---
title: "Air Brake Systems"
code: "DSL-160"
category: "diesel"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Studies the basic operational theory of pneumatic and air brake systems as used in heavy-duty and public transportation vehicles. Covers various air control valves, test system components, and advanced air system schematics. Teaches proper service and preventative maintenance of systems. Lecture 2 hours. Laboratory 2 hours. Total 4 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
